  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 349 AM MDT Wed Jul 22 2026\n\nEarly morning radar shows showers filtering into the South Hills \nregion from the south. Southwest flow will continue to stream deep \nmonsoonal moisture into Southeast Idaho today, which will support \nscattered showers and thunderstorms. Activity will taper off early \nthis morning before a shortwave feature enhances another round of \norganized showers and thunderstorms this afternoon and evening. \nStorms will be wet today, capable of producing heavy rain and \nlocalized flooding. The FLOOD WATCH remains in effect for the east \nand southeast highlands, where confidence in flash flooding impacts \nis highest, as well as for the Wapiti burn scar due to the risk of \ndebris flows. Storms will be capable of producing 35 to 45 mph \noutflow winds, as well. Today's high temperatures will be noticeably \ncooler, running around normal to slightly below normal with \nwidespread 80s across the low elevations. With the exception of some \nlingering chances for isolated showers and storms late week, \nconditions will trend dry with above normal temperatures returning \nfor the end of the week and weekend.",
